*/}

    <section
      class="feature-grid"
      id="features"
      aria-label="VoxTerm features"
    >
      <article class="feature-card wide reveal">
        <p class="card-kicker">Terminal Sessions</p>

        <h3>Keep multiple terminals alive without throwing away your state</h3>

        <p>
          Create named sessions from saved hosts, run them side by side, minimize
          them, restore them later, and manage their connection state from a
          dedicated sessions experience. VoxTerm keeps each terminal view
          persistent so the buffer survives while you move elsewhere in the app.
        </p>

        <div class="chip-row">
          <span>Multiple Sessions</span>
          <span>Minimize & Restore</span>
          <span>Persistent Terminal Buffer</span>
          <span>Session Detail</span>
          <span>Active Session Sheet</span>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article class="feature-card reveal">
        <p class="card-kicker">SSH Hosts</p>

        <h3>Save the machines behind your work and reconnect quickly</h3>

        <p>
          Add and manage SSH hosts with names, hostnames, usernames, ports,
          favorites, and password or key authentication. Passwords can be kept in
          Keychain when you choose, letting familiar machines stay ready without
          making you re-enter the same connection details every time.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="feature-card reveal">
        <p class="card-kicker">Projects</p>

        <h3>Turn recurring development work into reusable terminal workspaces</h3>

        <p>
          Create projects with a name, purpose, host, working directory, notes,
          icon, and reusable command set. Search them, favorite them, duplicate
          them, archive and restore them, or open the full project detail
          experience when you need the context behind the terminal session.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="feature-card reveal">
        <p class="card-kicker">Commands & Tokens</p>

        <h3>Make repeatable commands flexible enough for real work</h3>

        <p>
          Save commands at the session or project level, name and explain them,
          edit them later, and run them directly from the terminal workflow.
          Commands can include named tokens that VoxTerm asks you to replace at
          execution time, so one saved command can adapt to changing values.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="feature-card reveal">
        <p class="card-kicker">SFTP Workspace</p>

        <h3>Browse, create, rename, delete, and edit remote files from the same connection</h3>

        <p>
          Open the SFTP workspace from a connected terminal to navigate remote
          directories with breadcrumbs and search, create files and folders,
          rename or delete items, refresh directory contents, and open editable
          files without leaving the host you are already working on.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="feature-card wide reveal">
        <p class="card-kicker">Remote Code Editor</p>

        <h3>Edit code on the remote machine with an editor built into VoxTerm</h3>

        <p>
          Remote files open in a Runestone-powered editor with line numbers,
          line wrapping, monospaced editing, syntax highlighting, manual save,
          debounced auto-save, and external-change detection before overwriting a
          file that changed remotely. The same SFTP connection bridges the editor
          directly back to the machine.
        </p>

        <div class="reader-preview">
          <div class="reader-preview-top">
            <span>Remote Editing</span>
            <strong>Auto-save enabled</strong>
          </div>

          <div class="reader-bar">
            <span></span>
          </div>

          <div class="reader-meta">
            <span>Syntax Highlighting</span>
            <span>Line Numbers</span>
            <span>Change Detection</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </article>
    </section>

    <section class="spotlight reveal">
      <div class="spotlight-copy">
        <p class="eyebrow">Terminal Controls</p>

        <h2>Make a touch keyboard behave more like the keyboard a terminal expects</h2>

        <p>
          VoxTerm adds a terminal-focused accessory toolbar with Done, Ctrl, Esc,
          Tab, saved Commands, and common control characters. The command field
          stays connected to the live terminal while session and project commands
          remain one tap away when repetitive shell work needs to move faster.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="share-demo" aria-label="VoxTerm terminal control preview">
        <span class="share-pill">Terminal Toolbar</span>

        <h4>Keep shell controls within reach.</h4>

        <div class="share-row">
          <span>Ctrl / Esc / Tab</span>
          <strong>Terminal-specific keys on mobile</strong>
        </div>

        <div class="share-row">
          <span>Commands</span>
          <strong>Run saved session or project commands</strong>
        </div>

        <div class="share-row">
          <span>Directory</span>
          <strong>See current remote context</strong>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="details-section reveal">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <p class="eyebrow">Everything Else</p>

        <h2>Open each part of the VoxTerm experience</h2>
      </div>

      <div class="details-list">
        <details open>
          <summary>
            <span>
              <b>Home Dashboard</b>
              <small>Return to recent hosts, active sessions, projects, and shortcuts</small>
            </span>
          </summary>

          <p>
            The Home page surfaces recent hosts, active sessions, recent projects,
            and quick actions for creating or returning to the parts of VoxTerm
            you use most. Active-session state is visible throughout the main app
            so live connections never disappear into the background.
          </p>
        </details>

        <details>
          <summary>
            <span>
              <b>Session Details & Active Session Management</b>
              <small>Inspect, restore, disconnect, minimize, and remove sessions</small>
            </span>
          </summary>

          <p>
            Sessions have both a dedicated list and detail flow, while the active
            sessions sheet makes current connections accessible from elsewhere in
            the app. You can resume, minimize, disconnect, or remove sessions and
            create additional sessions from saved hosts.
          </p>
        </details>

        <details>
          <summary>
            <span>
              <b>Authentication & Sign-In</b>
              <small>Use SSH credentials and Voxiverse account authentication where needed</small>
            </span>
          </summary>

          <p>
            SSH hosts support password or key authentication, with optional
            Keychain storage for remembered passwords. VoxTerm also includes its
            own sign-in experience for the account-facing parts of the app.
          </p>
        </details>

        <details>
          <summary>
            <span>
              <b>Project Search, Filters & Editing</b>
              <small>Find, organize, duplicate, archive, and revise reusable workspaces</small>
            </span>
          </summary>

          <p>
            Search projects by name or details and filter between active,
            favorite, and archived workspaces. Project editor and detail views
            handle the deeper configuration, while context actions support
            duplication, favoriting, archiving, restoring, and deletion.
          </p>
        </details>

        <details>
          <summary>
            <span>
              <b>Command Editor & Token Replacement</b>
              <small>Build reusable commands that can request values before they run</small>
            </span>
          </summary>

          <p>
            The command editor keeps names, shell commands, explanations, and
            execution behavior together. Insert named token placeholders while
            editing and let VoxTerm collect replacement values before running the
            command from either project or terminal command flows.
          </p>
        </details>

        <details>
          <summary>
            <span>
              <b>SFTP Browser & File Operations</b>
              <small>Navigate remote folders and manage files from iPhone or iPad</small>
            </span>
          </summary>

          <p>
            The SFTP browser adapts between an iPhone navigation stack and an
            iPad split view. Search the current directory, follow breadcrumb paths,
            create files or folders, rename and delete items, refresh contents,
            and open files directly into the remote editor.
          </p>
        </details>

        <details>
          <summary>
            <span>
              <b>Themes, Profile & Settings</b>
              <small>Customize the terminal environment and account-facing experience</small>
            </span>
          </summary>

          <p>
            VoxTerm includes dedicated Profile and Settings areas, plus selectable
            themes with terminal previews and color swatches. Theme changes flow
            through the app's terminal, host, session, project, and editor
            interfaces so the workspace can match the environment you prefer.
          </p>
        </details>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="community-banner reveal">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Built Around Real Remote Work</p>

        <h2>The command line is only one part of a useful mobile development workspace.</h2>

        <p>
          VoxTerm is built around the full context of remote development: hosts you
          trust, sessions you keep alive, projects you return to, commands you
          repeat, files you need to inspect or edit, and a terminal environment
          that should remain comfortable across all of it.
        </p>
      </div>

      <a class="primary-button raised-button" href="https://discord.gg/SaZJKF3d9U">
        Join the Community
      </a>
    </section>

    <section class="cta-section reveal">
      <p class="eyebrow">Explore VoxTerm</p>

      <h2>Keep a complete remote development workflow within reach.</h2>

      <p>
        Learn more about VoxTerm, report a problem, share an idea, or reach out
        directly through Voxiverse Support.
      </p>

      <div class="cta-grid">
        <a
          href="https://github.com/asteriasmoons/VoxTerm/issues/1"
          class="cta-card"
        >
          <span class="cta-kicker">Report an Issue</span>

          <h2>VoxTerm Bug Reports</h2>

          <span class="cta-button">Open Reports</span>
        </a>

        <a href="/github" class="cta-card">
          <span class="cta-kicker">Ideas & Discussions</span>

          <h2>Voxiverse on GitHub</h2>

          <span class="cta-button">Open GitHub</span>
        </a>

        <a href="/contact" class="cta-card">
          <span class="cta-kicker">Need Help?</span>

          <h2>Contact Support</h2>

          <span class="cta-button">Get Support</span>
        </a>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</DocsLayout>

<script>
  const revealItems = document.querySelectorAll(".reveal");

  const revealObserver = new IntersectionObserver(
    (entries) => {
      entries.forEach((entry) => {
        if (entry.isIntersecting) {
          entry.target.classList.add("is-visible");
          revealObserver.unobserve(entry.target);
        }
      });
    },
    { threshold: 0.12 }
  );

  revealItems.forEach((item) => revealObserver.observe(item));

  document
    .querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>("[data-voxterm-gallery]")
    .forEach((gallery) => {
      const track =
        gallery.querySelector<HTMLElement>("[data-gallery-track]");

      const slides = Array.from(
        gallery.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>(".gallery-slide")
      );

      const previousButton =
        gallery.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>(
          "[data-gallery-previous]"
        );

      const nextButton =
        gallery.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>(
          "[data-gallery-next]"
        );

      const count =
        gallery.querySelector<HTMLElement>("[data-gallery-count]");

      const progress =
        gallery.querySelector<HTMLElement>("[data-gallery-progress]");

      if (
        !track ||
        !slides.length ||
        !previousButton ||
        !nextButton
      ) {
        return;
      }

      let currentIndex = 0;
      let autoplay: number | undefined;
      let dragStartX = 0;

      const updateGallery = () => {
        track.style.transform =
          `translateX(-${currentIndex * 100}%)`;

        slides.forEach((slide, index) => {
          slide.classList.toggle(
            "is-active",
            index === currentIndex
          );
        });

        if (count) {
          count.textContent =
            `${currentIndex + 1} / ${slides.length}`;
        }

        if (progress) {
          progress.style.width =
            `${((currentIndex + 1) / slides.length) * 100}%`;
        }
      };

      const showSlide = (index: number) => {
        currentIndex =
          (index + slides.length) % slides.length;

        updateGallery();
      };

      const startAutoplay = () => {
        window.clearInterval(autoplay);

        autoplay = window.setInterval(
          () => showSlide(currentIndex + 1),
          4200
        );
      };

      const stopAutoplay = () => {
        window.clearInterval(autoplay);
      };

      nextButton.addEventListener("click", () => {
        showSlide(currentIndex + 1);
        startAutoplay();
      });

      previousButton.addEventListener("click", () => {
        showSlide(currentIndex - 1);
        startAutoplay();
      });

      gallery.addEventListener("pointerdown", (event) => {
        dragStartX = event.clientX;
        stopAutoplay();
      });

      gallery.addEventListener("pointerup", (event) => {
        const deltaX = event.clientX - dragStartX;

        if (Math.abs(deltaX) > 40) {
          showSlide(
            currentIndex + (deltaX < 0 ? 1 : -1)
          );
        }

        startAutoplay();
      });

      gallery.addEventListener(
        "mouseenter",
        stopAutoplay
      );

      gallery.addEventListener(
        "mouseleave",
        startAutoplay
      );

      gallery.addEventListener(
        "focusin",
        stopAutoplay
      );

      gallery.addEventListener(
        "focusout",
        startAutoplay
      );

      window.addEventListener(
        "resize",
        updateGallery
      );

      updateGallery();
      startAutoplay();
    });
</script>

<style>
  .voxterm-page {
    position: relative;
    width: 100%;
    padding: 1rem 0 5rem;
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  .hero {
    position: relative;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns:
      minmax(0, 1.2fr)
      minmax(310px, 0.8fr);
    align-items: center;
    gap: 3rem;
    min-height: 620px;
    padding: 4rem 0;
  }

  .hero-copy,
  .hero-showcase {
    position: relative;
    z-index: 2;
  }

  .hero h1 {
    max-width: 860px;
    margin: 0 0 1.25rem;
    font-size: clamp(3rem, 7vw, 6.5rem);
    line-height: 0.96;
    letter-spacing: -0.055em;
  }

  .eyebrow,
  .card-kicker,
  .mini-label {
    margin: 0 0 0.85rem;
    font-size: 0.76rem;
    font-weight: 800;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }

  .hero-text,
  .intro-section p,
  .spotlight p,
  .community-banner p,
  .cta-section > p {
    max-width: 760px;
    font-size: 1.06rem;
  }

  .hero-actions {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.85rem;
    margin-top: 2rem;
  }

  .primary-button,
  .secondary-button {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    min-height: 50px;
    padding: 0.9rem 1.3rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    border-radius: 999px;
    color: var(--color-bg);
    text-decoration: none;
    transition:
      transform 0.2s ease,
      border-color 0.2s ease;
  }

  .primary-button {
    background: var(--accent-periwinkle);
  }

  .secondary-button {
    background: var(--surface-raised) !important;
    color: var(--color-text) !important;
  }

  .primary-button:hover,
  .secondary-button:hover {
    transform: translateY(-3px);
    border-color: var(--accent-periwinkle);
  }

  .hero-showcase {
    min-height: 410px;
  }

  .showcase-card,
  .floating-card,
  .feature-card,
  .share-demo,
  .details-list details,
  .community-banner,
  .cta-card {
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    background: var(--surface-standard);
    box-shadow: var(--glass-shadow-soft);
  }

  .main-card {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 55px 20px 55px 30px;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    justify-content: center;
    padding: 2rem;
    border-radius: 30px;
    transform: rotate(2deg);
  }

  .main-card h4 {
    max-width: 420px;
    margin: 0;
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3.6rem);
    line-height: 1.05;
  }

  .progress-line {
    height: 10px;
    margin: 1.75rem 0;
    border-radius: 999px;
    background: var(--surface-raised);
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  .progress-line span {
    display: block;
    width: 72%;
    height: 100%;
    border-radius: inherit;
    background: var(--accent-periwinkle);
    animation: pulse-width 3s ease-in-out infinite;
  }

  .showcase-stats {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 1rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }

  .showcase-stats b {
    color: var(--color-text);
  }

  .floating-card {
    position: absolute;
    z-index: 3;
    padding: 1rem 1.15rem;
    border-radius: 18px;
    animation: float 5s ease-in-out infinite;
  }

  .floating-card span {
    display: block;
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }

  .floating-card strong {
    font-size: 0.92rem;
  }

  .floating-card-one {
    top: 0;
    right: 0;
  }

  .floating-card-two {
    bottom: 8px;
    left: 0;
    animation-delay: -2.4s;
  }

  @media (min-width: 901px) {
    :global(.content:has(.voxterm-page)) {
      max-width: 1280px;
      padding-inline: clamp(1.5rem, 3vw, 3rem);
    }

    .hero {
      grid-template-columns:
        minmax(0, 1fr)
        minmax(340px, 380px);
      gap: clamp(2rem, 3.5vw, 4rem);
      min-height: 610px;
      padding: 2.15rem 0 2.65rem;
    }

    .hero h1 {
      max-width: 840px;
      margin-bottom: 1rem;
      font-size: 4.15rem;
      line-height: 1;
      letter-spacing: 0;
    }

    .hero-text {
      max-width: 660px;
      font-size: 1rem;
    }

    .hero-actions {
      margin-top: 1.5rem;
    }

    .hero-showcase {
      align-self: center;
      justify-self: end;
      width: 100%;
      max-width: 380px;
      min-height: 430px;
    }

    .main-card {
      inset: 58px 16px 104px 16px;
      padding: 1.45rem;
      border-radius: 26px;
      transform: none;
    }

    .main-card h4 {
      max-width: 320px;
      font-size: 2.35rem;
    }

    .progress-line {
      margin: 1.2rem 0;
    }

    .showcase-stats {
      gap: 0.65rem 0.9rem;
      font-size: 0.9rem;
    }

    .floating-card-one {
      top: 0;
      right: 0;
      max-width: 282px;
    }

    .floating-card-two {
      bottom: 16px;
      left: 0;
      max-width: 292px;
    }
  }

  @media (min-width: 901px) and (max-width: 1160px) {
    .hero {
      grid-template-columns:
        minmax(0, 1fr)
        minmax(320px, 340px);
      gap: 2rem;
    }

    .hero h1 {
      font-size: 3.7rem;
    }

    .main-card h4 {
      font-size: 2.1rem;
    }
  }

  @media (min-width: 1400px) {
    .hero h1 {
      font-size: 4.75rem;
    }
  }

  .intro-section {
    max-width: 850px;
    padding: 4rem 0 2rem;
  }

  .intro-section h2,
  .gallery-heading h2,
  .spotlight h2,
  .details-section h2,
  .community-banner h2,
  .cta-section h2 {
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3.6rem);
    line-height: 1.05;
  }

  .voxterm-gallery-section {
    position: relative;
    padding: 2rem 0 3.25rem;
  }

  .gallery-heading {
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
  }

  .voxterm-gallery {
    position: relative;
    width: min(100%, 430px);
    margin: 0 auto;
